; Lock-on. A TOGGLE, not a hold: press to lock, press again to let go, press
; with nothing lockable to put the camera back behind the hero.
; scripts/targeting/targeting.gd owns that.
;
; On the pad this is the TOGGLE HALF ONLY -- R3, button 8, JOY_BUTTON_RIGHT_STICK.
; A thumb already resting on the right stick should not have to travel to
; recentre what that stick just moved, which is the one thing R3 is good for.
;
; The pad's Z is the LEFT TRIGGER, and it is bound to `shield` -- one pull, all
; four of the things OOT's Z did. See the note there. Both routes reach the same
; lock; they differ in what LETTING GO means. The trigger's lock drops with the
; trigger; R3's is a standing decision and survives it (`_lock_from_shield` in
; targeting.gd is what keeps a guard from silently disarming an R3 lock).
;
; The trigger was briefly bound here too, as a bare recentre, with the shield
; pushed up onto LB. That split is undone: it asked the player which of Z's four
; behaviours they wanted before they had learned that they are one behaviour.
z_target={
"deadzone": 0.2,
"events": [Object(InputEventMouseButton,"resource_local_to_scene":false,"resource_name":"","device":-1,"window_id":0,"alt_pressed":false,"shift_pressed":false,"ctrl_pressed":false,"meta_pressed":false,"button_mask":0,"position":Vector2(0, 0),"global_position":Vector2(0, 0),"factor":1.0,"button_index":3,"canceled":false,"pressed":false,"double_click":false,"script":null)
, Object(InputEventKey,"resource_local_to_scene":false,"resource_name":"","device":-1,"window_id":0,"alt_pressed":false,"shift_pressed":false,"ctrl_pressed":false,"meta_pressed":false,"pressed":false,"keycode":0,"physical_keycode":81,"key_label":0,"unicode":0,"location":0,"echo":false,"script":null)
, Object(InputEventJoypadButton,"resource_local_to_scene":false,"resource_name":"","device":-1,"button_index":8,"pressure":0.0,"pressed":false,"script":null)
]
}
; Attack is X/Square -- button 2, "Left Action". It moved off A because A had to
; become the USE button (see `use_item` below), and because the sword is the one
; thing in this game that is never put away: OOT keeps it on B forever and puts
; the items on the C-pad, and the whole reason an item can be drawn here without
; getting stuck is that a different button always swings.
;
; There is no `heavy_attack` any more. The heavy is the CHARGE: tap X for the
; light chain, hold X to wind up, release to swing it. One button, and the cost
; is time rather than a second thing to reach for -- which is the arrangement
; every Zelda spin attack has used. hero_combat.gd owns the hold clock.
attack={
"deadzone": 0.2,
"events": [Object(InputEventMouseButton,"resource_local_to_scene":false,"resource_name":"","device":-1,"window_id":0,"alt_pressed":false,"shift_pressed":false,"ctrl_pressed":false,"meta_pressed":false,"button_mask":0,"position":Vector2(0, 0),"global_position":Vector2(0, 0),"factor":1.0,"button_index":1,"canceled":false,"pressed":false,"double_click":false,"script":null)
, Object(InputEventJoypadButton,"resource_local_to_scene":false,"resource_name":"","device":-1,"button_index":2,"pressure":0.0,"pressed":false,"script":null)
]
}
; Use is the RIGHT TRIGGER -- JoyAxis 5 (TRIGGER_RIGHT), an InputEventJoypadMotion
; like the sticks, so the 0.2 deadzone is how far it travels before it counts.
; It is the "do the thing you are holding" button: it fires the bow or the
; hookshot when one is drawn, and with the sword out and something locked it is
; the lunge. With the sword out and nothing locked it does nothing, deliberately
; -- that is OOT's A exactly, where the jump attack only exists under Z.
;
; THE TWO TRIGGERS ARE THE PAIR, which is the whole reason it is here. BOTW puts
; the shield on ZL and the drawn item on ZR, and it is right: the left index
; finger holds a stance and the right index finger fires what that stance is
; aimed at. Aiming a bow with the left trigger and looSing it with a thumb makes
; you let go of the stick that was aiming.
;
; It lived on A/Cross before that, and the face buttons are now all swings and
; verbs -- attack on X, roll on B, interact on A. A is the button you press at a
; chest; it should not also be the button that looses an arrow through it.
;
; Keyboard is F, inherited from the heavy it replaced: left hand, without
; leaving WASD.
use_item={
"deadzone": 0.2,
"events": [Object(InputEventKey,"resource_local_to_scene":false,"resource_name":"","device":-1,"window_id":0,"alt_pressed":false,"shift_pressed":false,"ctrl_pressed":false,"meta_pressed":false,"pressed":false,"keycode":0,"physical_keycode":70,"key_label":0,"unicode":0,"location":0,"echo":false,"script":null)
, Object(InputEventJoypadMotion,"resource_local_to_scene":false,"resource_name":"","device":-1,"axis":5,"axis_value":1.0,"script":null)
]
}
; Block is the other half of the mouse: LMB swings, RMB raises the shield. It
; used to be K and Shift only, with RMB on z_target, and nobody found it -- the
; lock-on moved to the middle button, which is the thing you can afford to hide.
;
; ON THE PAD THIS IS OOT'S Z, and it is the whole of it. The LEFT TRIGGER --
; JoyAxis 4 (TRIGGER_LEFT), an InputEventJoypadMotion like the sticks, so the
; 0.2 deadzone is how far the trigger travels before it counts as pressed.
;
; One pull does four things, because in the source material they were never four
; things:
;   - raises the shield                       (hero_combat)
;   - acquires the best target                (targeting.gd `_read_guard`)
;   - pins the facing, so the stick strafes   (Hero._tick_camera_facing)
;   - and with NOTHING lockable, puts the camera back behind the hero.
; Let go and all four drop. An index finger on a shoulder is exactly what Z was.
;
; It spent one commit on LB (button 9) with the trigger reassigned to a bare
; recentre. That was a mistake and this is the undo: guarding, looking at the
; thing you are guarding against, and facing down an empty corridor are one
; intention, and splitting them across two fingers made the player choose.
;
; HELD, and polled with is_action_pressed -- the axis reports its travel through
; the same deadzone a button's 0/1 goes through, so nothing downstream in
; hero_combat cares which kind of event it is.
shield={
"deadzone": 0.2,
"events": [Object(InputEventMouseButton,"resource_local_to_scene":false,"resource_name":"","device":-1,"window_id":0,"alt_pressed":false,"shift_pressed":false,"ctrl_pressed":false,"meta_pressed":false,"button_mask":0,"position":Vector2(0, 0),"global_position":Vector2(0, 0),"factor":1.0,"button_index":2,"canceled":false,"pressed":false,"double_click":false,"script":null)
, Object(InputEventJoypadMotion,"resource_local_to_scene":false,"resource_name":"","device":-1,"axis":4,"axis_value":1.0,"script":null)
]
}
; Roll is B/Circle, Elden Ring's arrangement, and is unchanged.
;
; Interact is BACK on A/Cross -- button 0, the thumb's rest position, which is
; where every game in this genre puts "talk to that / open that". It was pushed
; up to Y for one reason and one reason only: `use_item` was on A, and sharing A
; between "open the chest" and "loose an arrow" would have fired both off one
; press (hero_combat polls its buttons every physics frame, with no disarmed
; edge to protect it). `use_item` is on the RIGHT TRIGGER now, so the collision
; is gone and A goes back to the button it should always have been.
;
; It still shares A with ui_accept, and that has always been safe for a
; different reason: trade_screen's accept edge starts DISARMED, so the press
; that opens a screen cannot also confirm inside it.
;
; Y/Triangle is now free. Leave it that way until something earns it -- an empty
; button is honest, a button bound to a dead action is a bug report.
context={
"deadzone": 0.2,
